/**
 * The `venue-names` table (ADR-0064 stage 4, decisions of 31.10 and 1.11): Lublin 2077's name for
 * every named venue of the map. A chain gets a play on words a Lubliner knows at once, never a
 * letter off its mark, the same sound, a word of it, a translation of it or the motif of its logo
 * or slogan; one chain, one name. A local venue gets a name after its kind and a place of the
 * 2077 street (generated by kind and place, then checked), never its real name, a translation of
 * it or the real one with a tag stuck on (ADR-0058: no trademarks). Data, not
 * texts for the catalogs: names stay as they are in every language (ADR-0056 keeps the city's
 * signs Polish). The colour is the real sign's, by eye, where the chain or the venue has a known
 * one; the importer brings it to the kit's neon (ADR-0022). Spelt in `SIGN_GLYPHS`.
 */
